From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:28:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Run the IndexedDB integration tests on every backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tests/indexeddb.rs drives the storage threads the way script does, so it
tested whichever IndexedDB executor the build ran on: SQLite on the host,
and on a device with both backends only RDB, which the
storage_ohos_rdb_backend_enabled pref selects by default.

Each test is now a plain function, and `backend_tests!` defines a
`#[test]` for it per backend compiled in, in a module named after the
backend (`indexeddb::sqlite::…`, `indexeddb::rdb::…`). The wrapper
takes the test lock and sets the pref before the test opens its
databases, so with both backends compiled in each test runs once on
SQLite and once on RDB; with one backend the pref has no effect.

Validation: host `cargo nextest run -p servo-storage -p servo-storage-traits`: 71 passed, the 11 integration tests as `indexeddb::sqlite::…`. DAYU200 with both backends (`./mach test-unit --ohos -p servo-storage -- --features ohos-rdb-backend --status-level all`): 111 passed, each integration test once as `indexeddb::sqlite::…` and once as `indexeddb::rdb::…`; RDB only: 69 passed; one documented skip in each.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and run on the host and the DAYU200 by the agent, and run again by a later agent session after review fixes to the previous commit)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
